// Regla Sigma: proc_creation_macos_system_profiler_discovery.yml
// ID Sigma: 4809c683-059b-4935-879d-36835986f8cf
// Título: System Information Discovery Using System_Profiler
// Descripción: Detects the execution of "system_profiler" with specific "Data Types" that have been seen being used by threat actors and malware. It provides system hardware and software configuration information.
This process is primarily used for system information discovery. However, "system_profiler" can also be used to determine if virtualization software is being run for defense evasion purposes.

// Fecha de creación: 2024-01-02
// Fecha de modificación: 
// Aplica a: Producto: macos | Categoría: process_creation
// Producto: macos
// Categoría: process_creation
// Servicio: 
// Nivel: medium
// Pipeline: microsoft_xdr
// Ruta original: C:\SigmaLab\sigma\rules\macos\process_creation\proc_creation_macos_system_profiler_discovery.yml
// Requiere validación en el entorno de destino.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "/system_profiler" or ProcessCommandLine contains "system_profiler") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "SPApplicationsDataType" or ProcessCommandLine contains "SPHardwareDataType" or ProcessCommandLine contains "SPNetworkDataType" or ProcessCommandLine contains "SPUSBDataType")
